<title>GERMANY: D.Babcock to take restructuring charge.</title>
<headline>D.Babcock to take restructuring charge.</headline>
<dateline>OBERHAUSEN, Germany 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Babcock AG said on Monday it would take a larger restructuring charge than expected from the closure of its Magdeburg plant and other key changes stemming from a strategic business plan set in July.</p>
<p>The company said in a regulatory news release that personnel changes in its piping unit and at its U.S. operations would also cost more than originally estimated.</p>
<p>&quot;The planned extent of the restructuring costs will therefore be exceeded through further provisions,&quot; the company statement said.</p>
